 "notes": "Libretto by Luigi Illica and Giuseppe Giacosa (1896). Words follow the Ricordi vocal score's spelling and punctuation (Sciampagna, Berlingaccio, m'inpingua as printed (m'in-pin-gua; the libretto has m'impingua), minister, mister, cimiter, ber, Rigodone, the French dance calls Balancez! and Rond, and the runs of dots after vedrò). Spoken words (printed without noteheads, written with cross noteheads): Marcello's \"La prego.\", Colline's \"Balancez!\" and Schaunard's \"Assaggia.\". Lallera is the friends' tra-la-la for the dance. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, words sung on one note joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ, intervocalic s voiced. Translation literal, for meaning.",
